wikipedia_extract: 'USS Phoenix (CL-46) was a light cruiser of the Brooklyn class.
  She was the third Phoenix of the United States Navy. After World War II the ship
  was transferred to Argentina in 1951 and was named General Belgrano in 1956. General
  Belgrano was sunk during the Falklands War in 1982 by the British submarine HMS
  Conqueror.

  She was laid down on 15 April 1935 by the New York Shipbuilding Corporation, Camden,
  New Jersey; launched on 13 March 1938; sponsored by Mrs. Dorothea Kays Moonan; and
  commissioned at Philadelphia Navy Yard on 3 October 1938. Her name was in honor
  of the capital city of the state of Arizona.'
